Author:     adamv-symbolica <adam.vandervorst@symbolica.ai>
AuthorDate: Fri Oct 30 12:21:44 2026 +0000
Commit:     adamv-symbolica <adam.vandervorst@symbolica.ai>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 30 12:21:44 2026 +0000

    Make restrict of a dense node by a list/tiny node visit only the restrictor's branches
    
    `prestrict_abstract` scanned every child of the (up to 256 wide) dense
    `self` node and asked the list or tiny `other` node about each one, so a
    restriction by a sparse map cost O(width of the LHS) per node it passed
    through.  It now intersects `self`'s mask with `other`'s branch mask and
    visits only the overlap, which is at most 2 bytes.  `TinyRefNode` gets a
    real `node_branches_mask` to supply that mask.
    
    Adds benches/restrict.rs, sweeping LHS/RHS branching, depth below the
    cut-off on either side, cut-off depth, overlap, and LHS/RHS size.
    LHS branching 256 goes from 554 to 47 µs (flat in branching now), and a
    1M key random LHS restricted by 64 keys from 37 to 3.8 µs.
    
    Adds an oracle test restricting wide maps by a few of their own paths,
    cut short, extended, diverging, or whole, through `restrict`,
    `WriteZipper::restrict` (including its status), and `restricting`.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

